question:
Find c so that the function is continuous on R:
f(x) = { (x^2 - 1) / √(x^2 + 2x + 1)   if x < -1;
         2x + c                        if x ≥ -1 }

Solve for z from the system:
{
  x - y + 2z + 3w = 2
  x - y + 3z + 2w = 5
  2x - 2y + 4z + 7w = 5
}

Solve the following the linear system:
{
  x - y - z = 1
  x + z = 2
  y - 2z = 5
}

Which of the following is a subspace of R^3?
(i) U = {(a + b, 3a - b, 2a + b) | a, b ∈ R}
(ii) U = {(a, b, c) | a^2 + b^2 - c^2 = 0}

Which of the following subsets are independent?
(i) {[0, 1, 2], [1, 1, 0], [2, 2, 1]}
(ii) {[1, 2], [2, 1]}
(iii) {[0, 1], [2, 3], [1, 4]}
